---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  FormCompositions,
  FormLayouts,
  FormPlayground,
  FormSections,
  FormSubmitStates,
  FormValidation,
} from '../../components/FormDemo';
---

<Docs title="Form">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Form</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A form that locks its fields while saving, moves focus to the first error, and ends with a save area that explains
    why it cannot save yet.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <FormPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section" id="form-usage">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Form usage"
      code={`import { Form, FormFooter, FormSection } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/form";
import { Field } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/field";
import { Input } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/input";

<Form label="Change interval" disabled={saving} onSubmit={() => {
  if (error) { setChecked(true); return "invalid"; }
  save(minutes);
}}>
  <FormSection title="Scheduled trigger" description="Start this agent on an interval.">
    <Field label="Run every" required error={checked ? error : undefined}>
      <Input type="number" value={minutes} onChange={…} />
    </Field>
  </FormSection>
  <FormFooter
    dirty={minutes !== saved}
    note="Saving makes you the sponsor."
    submit={{
      label: "Save interval",
      pendingLabel: "Saving interval…",
      state: saving ? { kind: "busy" } : { kind: "ready" },
    }}
    cancel={{ kind: "reset", label: "Discard changes", onReset: reset }}
  />
</Form>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Form</code> renders a <code>noValidate</code> form and prevents the browser submit. Return{' '}
      <code>"invalid"</code> from <code>onSubmit</code>
      after you show errors; the form then scrolls to and focuses the first control with{' '}
      <code>aria-invalid="true"</code>. <code>disabled</code>
      locks every <code>Field</code>, <code>ChoiceGroup</code>, and
      <code>CheckboxField</code> inside. <code>label</code> names the form.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>FormSection</code> is a bordered region named by its
      <code>title</code>, or by <code>label</code> when set. It takes an optional
      <code>description</code>, a <code>meta</code> badge such as
      <code>3 / 20</code>, an <code>id</code> to jump to, and
      <code>level</code>
      <code>2</code> or <code>3</code> for the heading.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Validation and recovery</h2>
    <p>
      Clear a field and save. Focus moves to the first error, the footer shows a summary, and Discard changes restores
      the saved values. While saving, the fields lock and Discard changes hides.
    </p>
    <FormValidation client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Footer layouts</h2>
    <p>
      <code>bar</code> sits under a divider for page and section forms.
      <code>stack</code> uses full-width large buttons for sign-in, onboarding, and dialogs. <code>compact</code> fits
      chat cards: it hides the status line from sight, and its children sit beside the buttons instead of below them.
    </p>
    <FormLayouts client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="form-integrations">
    <h2 class="section-title">Submit states</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Blocked submit with a fix"
      code={`submit={{
  label: "Add Slack destination",
  pendingLabel: "Adding Slack destination…",
  state: team ? { kind: "ready" } : {
    kind: "blocked",
    reason: "Choose a destination team below first.",
    fix: { kind: "jump", label: "Choose a team", target: "slack-destination-team" },
  },
}}`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>busy</code> shows <code>pendingLabel</code> and sets
      <code>aria-busy</code>. <code>blocked</code> shows its
      <code>reason</code> under the buttons and links it with
      <code>aria-describedby</code>. Busy and blocked buttons stay focusable so keyboard users hear why. A{' '}
      <code>fix</code> adds a link button:
      <code>jump</code> focuses an element by id, <code>action</code> runs a callback, and <code>link</code> renders
      your router link.
      <code>dirty</code> shows Unsaved changes; a <code>reset</code> cancel shows only while dirty and not busy.
    </p>
    <FormSubmitStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sections</h2>
    <p>
      Meta badges count choices or items. The header wraps the badge under the title when the section is narrow. Long
      titles and descriptions wrap.
    </p>
    <FormSections client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="form-compositions">
    <h2 class="section-title">Compositions</h2>
    <p>
      <code>secondarySubmit</code> adds an outline submit such as Save draft; its
      <code>onSelect</code> runs before the form submits. A<code>leave</code> cancel renders a link. Pass{' '}
      <code>form</code> to put the footer outside its form, and <code>summary</code> to replace the status line with
      your own content. Footer children carry save feedback, alerts, and extra actions.
    </p>
    <FormCompositions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Name every form with <code>label</code> or a surrounding section. Errors render in a destructive{' '}
      <code>Alert</code>. Status lines fade in over 180ms and appear at once with reduced motion. Saving, routing, and
      data in these examples are sample code; the textarea is a docs-only stand-in.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
